bodyHtml: |
  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Lanterne is one of the two beaches the City of Nice reserves for dogs. It sits at the western end of the Promenade des Anglais, behind the Carras harbour, not far from the airport: a pebble site slightly away from the centre, more than a postcard beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to nice.fr, Plage de la Lanterne (400 Promenade des Anglais) is open to dogs year-round, like Lenval beach. Note: the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office lists it at 386 Promenade des Anglais; both sources refer to Plage de la Lanterne. The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office specifies the rule by category: category 3 dogs may be off-leash and swim, category 2 dogs must be muzzled and kept on a leash, and category 1 dogs are banned. It is not the city's only dog beach: Lenval is the other.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Plage de Lenval, closer to the centre, is Nice's other dog beach if you want a change of scenery.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>In Saint-Laurent-du-Var, right next door, Vespins beach also accepts dogs — handy if the Lanterne is crowded.</p>
